// TypeScript diagnostics for the test-runner half of the frontend.
//
// The e2e specs and the WebdriverIO configs used to sit outside every
// tsconfig in this package: `tsconfig.json` includes `src/**` only,
// `tsconfig.node.json` includes `vite.config.ts` only, and nothing
// named any of what the `include` below now does. `just ui-e2e` does
// not close that gap either — the
// runner hands the specs to tsx/esbuild, which erases types without
// checking them. So `just ui-check` reported zero errors over ~4200
// lines it had never looked at, and the first run under this config
// turned up seven real diagnostics in four files [measured 2026-08-12].
//
// # Why a second config rather than a wider `include`
//
// Adding `e2e/**` to `tsconfig.json` would pull `describe` / `it` /
// `browser` into scope for all of `src/**`, because the `types` below
// are ambient: application code could then reference a test-runner
// global and still type-check. Two configs keep the two global
// environments apart, which is the property worth protecting — a
// stray `browser` in a Svelte component has to stay an error.
//
// Both halves run under `npm run check` (see package.json `check:app`
// and `check:e2e`), so `just ui-check` fails on a type error in a spec.
//
// # `types`
//
// Explicit, because the two environments differ and the difference is
// the point. `@wdio/globals/types` supplies `$` / `$$` / `browser`,
// `@wdio/mocha-framework` the BDD globals, `expect-webdriverio` the
// matchers. `vite/client` is here for one reason: e2e-bench imports
// `../src/lib/dev/thumb-perf`, which reads `import.meta.env`. Under
// `tsconfig.json` that resolves through `src/vite-env.d.ts`, which this
// config does not include — so without `vite/client` the import fails
// with TS2339 on a file that is perfectly correct. Scoping the fix here
// keeps it out of `src/`, where nothing is wrong.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": true,
    "types": [
      "node",
      "vite/client",
      "@wdio/globals/types",
      "@wdio/mocha-framework",
      "expect-webdriverio"
    ]
  },
  "include": [
    "e2e/**/*.ts",
    "e2e-bench/**/*.ts",
    "e2e-teams/**/*.ts",
    "wdio.conf.ts",
    "wdio.bench.conf.ts",
    "wdio.teams.conf.ts"
  ]
}
